Below is a ready‑to‑use **GraphViz (DOT)** description that draws a colourful schematic of the **k‑fold cross‑validation** workflow that is typically used when you are tuning hyperparameters.  
The diagram shows the whole pipeline:

1. **Data → split into k folds**  
2. **Define a hyper‑parameter grid**  
3. **For each hyper‑parameter configuration** – run the **k‑fold CV** (train on k‑1 folds, validate on the remaining fold, repeat for all k folds)  
4. **Aggregate the scores** of each configuration  
5. **Select the best hyper‑parameters**

Feel free to copy the code into a file (e.g., `kfold_cv_tuning.dot`) and render it with  

```bash
dot -Tpng kfold_cv_tuning.dot -o kfold_cv_tuning.png
```

or any other GraphViz layout engine you prefer.

```dot
// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Colourful schematic of k‑fold cross‑validation for hyper‑tuning
// ---------------------------------------------------------------
digraph KFoldCV {
    // Layout left‑to‑right for a clean flow view
    rankdir=LR;
    splines=ortho;
    node [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, shape=box];

    // ---------- Nodes ----------
    // 1. Raw data
    data [label="Dataset\n(All samples)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#ADD8E6"];

    // 2. Splitting into k folds
    split [label="Split into k folds", shape=box, fillcolor="#FFD700"];

    // 3. Hyper‑parameter grid definition
    grid [label="Define Hyperparameter\nGrid", shape=box, fillcolor="#90EE90"];

    // 4. Example configurations (you can add more)
    cfgA [label="Config A\n(h₁, lr)", fillcolor="#FFB6C1"];
    cfgB [label="Config B\n(h₂, lr)", fillcolor="#FFB6C1"];

    // 5. k‑fold CV steps for each configuration
    //    (shown here for k = 3 – the pattern repeats for any k)
    cvA1 [label="Fold 1:\nTrain (k‑1) + Validate", fillcolor="#DDA0DD"];
    cvA2 [label="Fold 2:\nTrain (k‑1) + Validate", fillcolor="#DDA0DD"];
    cvA3 [label="Fold 3:\nTrain (k‑1) + Validate", fillcolor="#DDA0DD"];

    cvB1 [label="Fold 1:\nTrain (k‑1) + Validate", fillcolor="#DDA0DD"];
    cvB2 [label="Fold 2:\nTrain (k‑1) + Validate", fillcolor="#DDA0DD"];
    cvB3 [label="Fold 3:\nTrain (k‑1) + Validate", fillcolor="#DDA0DD"];

    // 6. Aggregate scores per configuration
    avgA [label="Average Score\n(Config A)", shape=box, fillcolor="#FFA07A"];
    avgB [label="Average Score\n(Config B)", shape=box, fillcolor="#FFA07A"];

    // 7. Final selection
    select [label="Select Best\nHyperparameters", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FF6347"];

    // ---------- Edges ----------
    // Data → split
    data -> split;

    // Split → grid definition
    split -> grid;

    // Grid → each hyper‑parameter configuration
    grid -> cfgA;
    grid -> cfgB;

    // ----- Path for Config A -----
    cfgA -> cvA1;
    cvA1 -> cvA2;
    cvA2 -> cvA3;
    cvA3 -> avgA;

    // ----- Path for Config B -----
    cfgB -> cvB1;
    cvB1 -> cvB2;
    cvB2 -> cvB3;
    cvB3 -> avgB;

    // Compare results & pick the winner
    avgA -> select;
    avgB -> select;
}
```

### How the diagram looks (conceptual)

```
+----------------+      +-------------------+      +-------------------+
|   Dataset      | ---> |  Split into k     | ---> |  Define Hyper-    |
| (all samples)  |      |  folds            |      |  parameter Grid   |
+----------------+      +-------------------+      +-------------------+
                                 |                         |
                                 v                         v
                        +-------------------+      +-------------------+
                        | Config A (h₁,lr)  |      | Config B (h₂,lr)  |
                        +-------------------+      +-------------------+
                                 |                         |
              +------------------+------------------+        |
              |                                     |        |
              v                                     v        |
        +-------------+                         +-------------+   |
        | Fold 1:     |                         | Fold 1:     |   |
        | Train (k‑1) |                         | Train (k‑1) |   |
        +-------------+                         +-------------+   |
              |                                     |        |
        +-------------+                         +-------------+   |
        | Fold 2:     |                         | Fold 2:     |   |
        | Train (k‑1) |                         | Train (k‑1) |   |
        +-------------+                         +-------------+   |
              |                                     |        |
        +-------------+                         +-------------+   |
        | Fold 3:     |                         | Fold 3:     |   |
        | Train (k‑1) |                         | Train (k‑1) |   |
        +-------------+                         +-------------+   |
              \____________________________________/             |
                                 |                           |
                                 v                           v
                        +-------------------+      +-------------------+
                        | Average Score    |      | Average Score    |
                        | (Config A/B)     |      | (Config A/B)     |
                        +-------------------+      +-------------------+
                                 |                           |
                                 +------------+--------------+
                                              |
                                            +-----+
                                            v
                                      +-----------------+
                                      | Select Best     |
                                      | Hyper‑parameters|
                                      +-----------------+
```

*Colors* (as defined in the DOT file) give a quick visual cue:

| Element                | Colour (hex) |
|------------------------|--------------|
| Dataset                | `#ADD8E6` (light blue) |
| Split into k folds    | `#FFD700` (gold) |
| Hyper‑parameter grid  | `#90EE90` (light green) |
| Configurations        | `#FFB6C1` (light pink) |
| Individual folds      | `#DDA0DD` (plum) |
| Averaged scores       | `#FFA07A` (sandy brown) |
| Final selection       | `#FF6347` (tomato) |

You can extend the diagram by adding more configurations, increasing the number of folds (just duplicate the `cvX` nodes), or inserting additional steps such as “Early stopping” or “Model persistence”. The structure stays the same: **data → split → hyper‑parameter search → k‑fold CV → aggregation → best parameters**. Happy visualising!

